{
  "abstract": "Entrywise estimates of quadratic jet determinants discard cancellation among derivative columns at a common node. We give a uniform scalar bound for the triangular row set used in explicit tenth-discriminant arguments, including its roughly twofold surplus of available columns. General Meixner weights produce a moment factor governed by affine composition on a reproducing-kernel space. A unitary kernel identity diagonalizes the infinite operator. A complementary determinant identity permits expanding affine maps in the finite polynomial factor, while a radius-dependent tilt retains part of the triangular constraint.\n\nAt the corrected basic parameters $D_0=5{,}000{,}000$, $K=31$ and $J/R\\leq .058$, the variable upper bound is below $0.167143014908$. The same-parameter monomial and pointwise disk bounds are $0.229844298595$ and $0.223725460514$. The arithmetic comparison gives a gap above $0.073226330038$ and positive logarithmic growth. The same fixed weights also restore two previously published class-number-one infinite-tail anchors, $794{,}000$ and $32{,}400$, with every norm-form branch loss retained. The latter gives $D<32{,}400$ and $\\log D_0=10.385913701780\\ldots$ using specified imported lemmas. A second spectral regime gives $0.260851688200$, compared with $0.317759188014$ for adapted monomial transport.\n\nExplicit errors cover factorials, signed row sums, column capacities, occupancy and radial bins. The arithmetic comparisons pay both identified radius corrections and a directed Mertens-constant allowance. A CPU replay checks exact rational certificates, finite matrix controls and complete branch accounting. Meixner orthogonality and the operator tools are classical; the contribution is their uniform application, including complementary products beyond the contraction range. Rank, radius and arithmetic lemmas remain identified imports. No finite census, bounded bridge or endpoint stronger than the previously published endpoints is claimed. Author checks are distinguished from independent review.",
